@njhill @yewentao256, could you review the round-seed handling in this fix for #61114?

Block verification currently reuses random draws when it revisits an uncommitted position in a later round. The fix separates acceptance and draft draws using the round's starting position, without adding scheduler state.

Real V2 model runs reproduce the bias before the fix and match the expected distribution afterward for both deterministic and probabilistic drafts. Standard verification output remains unchanged, and seeded block runs remain reproducible.

@njhill @yewentao256, #61161 now covers the direct DFlash2/LiLiCorr candidate walk and DSpark sampling paths as well. Each uses the same block-only round key, calculated inside the existing kernels without an additional round-position tensor.

#61153 addresses the same bug with an explicit round-position tensor. I ran the same deterministic/probabilistic multi-round distribution regression on both implementations, and both pass. The expanded #61161 also passes the existing candidate-cache, padding, graph-replay and watermark tests, and real V2 model generation preserves the corrected distribution and standard output.

Could you review #61161 for landing, particularly the in-kernel round-key handling and regression coverage?

